## 🎯 Project Overview

EduSync is a university student dashboard where students can view all their academic information across sessions — including circulars, attendance, marks, personal info, timetable, and university activities. There is **no sign-up flow**; student credentials are pre-seeded into the database by the university admin.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

Follow strict **MVC (Model-View-Controller)** architecture on the backend:
- **Model** → MongoDB schemas via Mongoose
- **View** → React 19 frontend (separate from backend)
- **Controller** → Express route handler functions (kept separate from route definitions)

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

### Frontend
- React 19 (Vite)
- React Router DOM v7
- Axios for API calls
- Tailwind CSS v4

### Backend
- Node.js + Express.js
- JWT (jsonwebtoken) for auth — access token + refresh token pattern
- bcryptjs for password hashing
- Mongoose (MongoDB ODM)
- dotenv, cors, cookie-parser

### Database
- MongoDB (local or Atlas)
- Credentials are **hardcoded/seeded** — no registration endpoint

